Description: Provides a comprehensive Bayesian framework for analyzing fear
    generalization data using latent mixture models. The package implements
    a two-phase experimental paradigm (conditioning and generalization) and
    identifies four distinct learning patterns: Non-Learners, Overgeneralizers,
    Physical Generalizers, and Perceptual Generalizers. Key features include
    parameter recovery analysis, perceptual noise modeling, automatic scale
    detection, and extensive visualization tools. Based on the computational
    model described in Yu et al. (2023) <doi:10.1038/s44271-023-00005-0>.
    The model incorporates Rescorla-Wagner learning, Shepard's similarity-based
    generalization, and hierarchical Bayesian inference to capture individual
    differences in fear learning mechanisms.
